course: dictionary
lesson: 4357
title: Gulp: swallowing fast, and feeling nervous
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Gulp can be a verb or a noun. As a verb, it means to swallow quickly in big mouthfuls, or to swallow suddenly because you feel nervous, scared or surprised. As a noun, a gulp is one big mouthful. Use the context to decide which meaning fits.
explain: «A thirsty camel can gulp around a hundred litres in a few minutes.» The camel is drinking, and the word «litres» and «thirsty» are clues. So gulp here means drink quickly in big mouthfuls. Now try a different sentence: «He gulped and stepped back.» No one is drinking, so the clue is the feeling. He was probably nervous or scared.
explain: Sometimes gulp is a noun: «She took a gulp of water.» The word «a» in front is a clue that gulp is a thing, a single mouthful. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Gulp means to swallow quickly in big mouthfuls, or to swallow suddenly when you feel nervous, scared or surprised.
fact: «A gulp of water» means one big mouthful, and here gulp is a noun.
fact: «Gulp air» means to breathe in air quickly, as a fish does when «a fish that keeps gulping at the surface may be short of oxygen».
fact: In comics, «Gulp!» is the sound of a nervous swallow.
fact: In health lessons, eat and drink slowly and do not gulp your food.
exercise: «A thirsty camel can gulp around a hundred litres in a few minutes.» What does gulp mean here? | *Drink quickly in big mouthfuls | Fall asleep under a tree | Breathe out slowly | Sing loudly with friends
exercise: «He gulped and stepped back from the dark cave.» What does gulped show about him? | He was cold and wet | He was very full and happy | He was going to sleep | *He was nervous or scared
exercise: «She took a gulp of water and felt better.» In this sentence, what kind of word is gulp? | *Noun | Verb | Adverb | Adjective
test: «A pufferfish gulps water into a stretchy stomach and swells to several times its size.» What does gulps mean here? | *Swallows large amounts of water quickly | Blows bubbles at the surface | Shakes its tail to swim | Sleeps under a rock
test: «A fish that keeps gulping at the surface may be short of oxygen.» Why might a fish gulp at the surface? | To find a mate | To keep warm in the sun | To sleep under the weed | *To breathe in air quickly
exam: Mia says, «He gulped and went pale when the teacher called his name.» What does gulped show? | *He was nervous | He was asleep | He was very hungry | He was painting a picture
